# QueryShield — example environment configuration
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IMPORTANT: Nothing in QueryShield reads these variables yet.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 1 is the project foundation only; there is no configuration loader, no
# database connectivity, no LLM client, and no cache. This file exists to
# DOCUMENT the environment variables the project is expected to use in later
# phases, and to give contributors a safe template.
#
# Usage (later phases): copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values.
#   cp .env.example .env
# `.env` is git-ignored and must NEVER be committed. These are placeholders
# only — do not put real API keys, passwords, or connection strings in THIS
# file.
#
# The exact variable names, defaults, and which are required vs. optional are
# finalized when the configuration layer is actually implemented (and recorded
# in docs/DECISIONS.md at that time). Treat the names below as illustrative.

# ---- LLM (Mistral, hosted API only; see ADR-0009) ----
# Hosted Mistral API key. Required once the LLM provider is implemented.
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=your-mistral-api-key-here
# Model name is configuration, never hard-coded. Example value only.
# MISTRAL_MODEL=mistral-large-latest

# ---- PostgreSQL ----
# Connection string for the target database. QueryShield expects to connect as
# a least-privilege role (see ADR-0002), not a superuser.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/queryshield

# ---- Cache (optional; see ADR-0007) ----
# Optional Redis URL for the secure, principal-partitioned cache. When unset, a
# future in-memory backend is expected to be used instead.
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

# ---- Application ----
# Log verbosity for the application's own logging. Example value only.
# QUERYSHIELD_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
